WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.029
Elvira is instantly recognizable by her enormous
black bouffant hairstyle and the plunging

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.980
neckline of her skin-tight vampiress gown.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.280
But behind the vamp-camp drag image is a real
woman with a storied history of her own.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.240
Here's the untold truth of Elvira.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.840
"Hi, this is Cassandra Peterson, better known
as Elvira, Mistress of the dark!"

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.800
As a child, young Cassandra Peterson suffered
scalding burns over 35% of her body, resulting

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.880
in the need to have a host of skin graft surgeries.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.259
This incident later caused her to feel marked,
both physically and otherwise, as different,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.600
and began her fascination with monsters and
outcasts.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.100
Growing up, Peterson developed a love of dancing
and decided to become a showgirl.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.840
Before she was even legally allowed to drink,
she had auditioned to be a professional dancer

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.420
and made the cut, traveling all around the
country dancing in bars and hotels.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.360
Because of this, she spent a great deal of
her teen years surrounded by gay men and drag

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:52.680
queens, an experience she credits wth giving
her the foundation for the enduring camp persona

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.660
that became Elvira.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.900
She also credits no less than Elvis himself
for advising her to leave her Las Vegas dancing

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.440
job and look for something bigger.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.340
"He is 100% responsible for me getting out
of Vegas and going on with my career.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.480
Elvis said to me, you don't want to stay here,
this is not a town you should be in."

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.480
After appearing in small roles in several
films and TV shows throughout the 1970s, Peteron

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.420
put the final piece of the puzzle together
in 1979 when she joined the famed Groundlings

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:23.620
theater troupe, whose alumni include such
luminaries as Kathy Griffin, Phil Hartman,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.280
and Jon Lovitz.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.020
Part of what makes Elvira so appealing is
the fact that she's a parody.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.430
But as always with parody, the person being
parodied didn't necessarily like it, leading

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.340
to a major lawsuit that almost derailed Elvira's
career before it began.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.780
In 1981, television producers looking to start
a weekly horror show hired 1950s horror host

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.260
Maila Nurmi to revive her character Vampira.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.840
After they parted ways due to creative differences,
however, the producers instead turned to Peterson

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.900
to host the show; she created Elvira for the
role, and an instant icon was born.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.000
Nurmi, however, thought Elvira's schtick was
way, way too close to Vampira and sued.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.900
In 1988 she made a rare appearance on a cable
talk show to discuss the case.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.140
"Cassandra Peterson claims that she has never
seen your show.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.020
Do you believe that?"

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:11.140
"I don't know for sure she saw them, except,
in February '82 she proceeded to emulate my

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.430
performance exactly."

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.280
"There are at least 80 similarities.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.400
It's identical, it's my show."

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.240
The judges ruled in Elvira's favor, in part
because Vampira herself was modeled after

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.840
Morticia from The Addams Family, but Nurmi
reportedly held a grudge for the rest of her

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.340
life.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:28.800
"Did anyone ever tell you you look like…"

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.280
"Vampira?"

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:30.920
"Yeah!"

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.200
"No."

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.500
To some viewers, Elvira is thoroughly all
about her sex appeal.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.560
For many others particularly young women and
gay men she is the marriage of sexiness, intelligence,

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.080
and campy humor.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.380
Some of that is Peterson's performance, but
a lot of it is Peterson's writing.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.040
Besides performing on screen, Peterson has
writing credits on most of her projects, including

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.000
the feature film Elvira: Mistress of the Dark.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.550
Along with her writing partner, fellow Groundlings
alum John Paragon, Peterson also authored

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.260
three novels credited to Elvira.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:02.660
And Peterson currently has an autobiography
slated to come out for Halloween 2020, which

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.880
she reportedly has been working on for 15
years!

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.780
Obviously, Peterson is best-known and best-loved
for her portrayal of the hilarious scream

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.980
queen, but she has also appeared in non-Elvira
roles, even after the character's debut.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:18.030
In Pee-Wee's Big Adventure, starring fellow
Groundlings alum Paul Reubens, Peterson played

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.931
a small but memorable role as "Biker Mama"
in a scene where Pee-Wee endears himself to

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.200
a seedy bar full of rough-and-tumble bikers.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:28.790
She's also done appropriately weird things
like the 2006 film Red Riding Hood, and the

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.790
absurd 2010 gorefest.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.480
2010 All About Evil.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.580
Those aren't her only non-Elvira roles, though.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.020
She also has a successful side gig as a voice
actor, working on everything from Super Robot

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.220
Monkey Team Hyperforce Go! to Teenage Mutant
Ninja Turtles, where she voiced the alien

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.040
Utrom Queen for six episodes.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.520
As Peterson approaches 70 years old, it is
remarkable how ageless she seems.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.640
She continues to don the Elvira costume with
grace, crediting her slim figure and youthful

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.450
appearance not on draining the blood of the
innocent as one might guess, but on good clean

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.240
living including yoga, regular running, and
maintaining a vegetarian diet.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.660
Her diet isn't just about keeping trim, however.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:06.060
She has publicly advocated for a vegetarian
diet for animal rights, even filming multiple

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.860
ads on behalf of People for the Ethical Treatment
of Animals.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.140
"You know, Bunny, I think you should give
back that leather coat you got for your birthday."

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.600
"Why, Elvira?"

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.200
"Because it looked better on the first cow!"

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.639
. These days, it seems she does eat some meat,
but she's still focused on keeping it primarily

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.540
fruit and veggies.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.900
It's just the latest unexpected life and career
twist for Peterson.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.690
All we can say is, we can't wait to see what
Elvira comes up with next.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.840
"Well, that's our show!

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:35.020
I hope you enjoyed watching it as much as
I did."

